517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (When using the Sound Mounds, it is important to have students apply sound mapping of the sounds that students hear within words. This in turn will promote the skill of orthographic mapping, which is a mental process that CANNOT be taugth to a child. The process of mapping words helps students to permanently retain certain spellings of words. )
/E (When using the Sound Mounds, it is important to have students apply sound mapping of the sounds that students hear within words. This in turn will promote the skill of orthographic mapping, which is a mental process that CANNOT be taugth to a child. The process of mapping words helps students to permanently retain certain spellings of words. )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
