/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (* The ou making the short O sound is a derivation from the Greek language. The spellings of these words changed within the Middle English age. The best way to help students teach these words is to promote sound mapping of words. You can teach these words as an irregular vowel pattern, and heart the tricky part.)
/E (* The ou making the short O sound is a derivation from the Greek language. The spellings of these words changed within the Middle English age. The best way to help students teach these words is to promote sound mapping of words. You can teach these words as an irregular vowel pattern, and heart the tricky part.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
910 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (* The letter O can also make the short U sound, representing the schwa. A lot of these words are high frequency words that students will need to map out and heart the word. The reasoning that these words make the schwa is because historically speaking these words were made easier to pronunciate. The schwa is an unstressed syllable within words that makes the short U sound. )
/E (* The letter O can also make the short U sound, representing the schwa. A lot of these words are high frequency words that students will need to map out and heart the word. The reasoning that these words make the schwa is because historically speaking these words were made easier to pronunciate. The schwa is an unstressed syllable within words that makes the short U sound. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
