/T (* The star above the open syllable a shows us that in a word with two or more syllables, the open syllable a grapheme will represent the long a sound when it is found at the ending of a syllable. Typically this syllable is not the ending syllable, but one the first syllable of the word. \(Ex. ba/by, la/dy, sha/dy\) )
/E (* The star above the open syllable a shows us that in a word with two or more syllables, the open syllable a grapheme will represent the long a sound when it is found at the ending of a syllable. Typically this syllable is not the ending syllable, but one the first syllable of the word. \(Ex. ba/by, la/dy, sha/dy\) )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
