/T (* The star above the open syllable i shows us that in a word with two or more syllables, the open syllable a grapheme will represent the long i sound. \(Ex. li/on, i/dea, pi/lot\) When open syllable e is used, typically the syllable is not the ending syllable of the word, but one the first syllables of the word. )
/E (* The star above the open syllable i shows us that in a word with two or more syllables, the open syllable a grapheme will represent the long i sound. \(Ex. li/on, i/dea, pi/lot\) When open syllable e is used, typically the syllable is not the ending syllable of the word, but one the first syllables of the word. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
