<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (* If we hear a /t/ at the end of a word, the grapheme igh will be used to reprsent the long I sound. The word high is one of the words that will end in the igh. You can teach this as a heart part depending on the grade level, however, it is a common grapheme that is used within our language.   )
/E (* If we hear a /t/ at the end of a word, the grapheme igh will be used to reprsent the long I sound. The word high is one of the words that will end in the igh. You can teach this as a heart part depending on the grade level, however, it is a common grapheme that is used within our language.   )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
