/E (*There are three main ways that we hear the /er/ sound produced. IR, UR, & ER are all graphemes that represent the /er/ phoneme. Out of the three, ER is the most frequently used grapheme, especially at the end of a word or syllable. \(Ex. per/fect, ti/ger, cop/per, ham/mer\) This does not mean that IR and UR cannot be found at the end of words or syllables.)
