<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (* If a word begins with OI \(ex. oil\), the student will use the oi unless the word has more than one syllable \(ex. oy/ster\). In oyster, the /oi/ syllable is by itself, so the grapheme to use would be oy. Also think of words like roy/al and loy/al. Remember, Sound Mounds represent words and syllables, so for these words be sure to use sound mapping and be sure to look at where the phoneme is heard in the word. However, there are exceptions to that rule like in the word poi/son. )
/E (* If a word begins with OI \(ex. oil\), the student will use the oi unless the word has more than one syllable \(ex. oy/ster\). In oyster, the /oi/ syllable is by itself, so the grapheme to use would be oy. Also think of words like roy/al and loy/al. Remember, Sound Mounds represent words and syllables, so for these words be sure to use sound mapping and be sure to look at where the phoneme is heard in the word. However, there are exceptions to that rule like in the word poi/son. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [29]
>>
