/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (* When /g/ is heard at the beginning of a word, the letters to follow will typically be a, o, and u. When the grapheme g is followed by an i, e, or y it most commonly makes the /j/ phoneme. \(Ex. gem, giraffe, gym\) This is known as the soft g. )
/E (* When /g/ is heard at the beginning of a word, the letters to follow will typically be a, o, and u. When the grapheme g is followed by an i, e, or y it most commonly makes the /j/ phoneme. \(Ex. gem, giraffe, gym\) This is known as the soft g. )
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [22 23]
>>
endobj
2606 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
