/T (* When /l/ is heard at the ending of words when following a short vowel, the grapheme will be ll \(pill, still, well\). If there is a long vowel or another vowel team, you will just use the l \(peel, sale, mail\). You can use the following chant when teaching the doubling of the f and the other letters this rule applies to:)
/E (* When /l/ is heard at the ending of words when following a short vowel, the grapheme will be ll \(pill, still, well\). If there is a long vowel or another vowel team, you will just use the l \(peel, sale, mail\). You can use the following chant when teaching the doubling of the f and the other letters this rule applies to:)
