/S /H3
/T (* When looking at words that begin with the letter w, often times the grapheme a that follows will produce the schwa sound. This is due to the changing of the sound throughout the history of the English language. The /w/ phoneme does influence mouth articulation too, so these can be taught as heart parts of words. \(want, watch, wash\) )
/E (* When looking at words that begin with the letter w, often times the grapheme a that follows will produce the schwa sound. This is due to the changing of the sound throughout the history of the English language. The /w/ phoneme does influence mouth articulation too, so these can be taught as heart parts of words. \(want, watch, wash\) )
/Pg 80 0 R
/K [8]
>>
