3729 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (* The phoneme /ch/ can be found at both the beginning and ending of words or syllables. When teaching the progression of this phonemes, the graphemes that go along with each of the graphemes that represent /ch/ should be considered.)
/E (* The phoneme /ch/ can be found at both the beginning and ending of words or syllables. When teaching the progression of this phonemes, the graphemes that go along with each of the graphemes that represent /ch/ should be considered.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
3730 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (When /ch/ comes at the beginning of a word, the most common graphemes that follow are long vowel teams or r-controlled vowels. This can be difficult for beginning readers who have not been introduced to these sounds yet. There are some words that do start with the ch grapheme and have short vowels follow like chip, chess, and chick. )
/E (When /ch/ comes at the beginning of a word, the most common graphemes that follow are long vowel teams or r-controlled vowels. This can be difficult for beginning readers who have not been introduced to these sounds yet. There are some words that do start with the ch grapheme and have short vowels follow like chip, chess, and chick. )
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
3731 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (When /ch/ comes at the ending of a word, the same concept follows as discussed above. We use the ch at the end of a word when there is a long vowel team, diphthong, or r-controlled vowel that comes before the /ch/. Examples of these words include peach and porch. However, if there is a consonant before the /ch/ as in punch, the ch grapheme will be used. )
/E (When /ch/ comes at the ending of a word, the same concept follows as discussed above. We use the ch at the end of a word when there is a long vowel team, diphthong, or r-controlled vowel that comes before the /ch/. Examples of these words include peach and porch. However, if there is a consonant before the /ch/ as in punch, the ch grapheme will be used. )
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
3732 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Another /ch/ ending is represented by the -tch grapheme. This only comes at the ending of words or syllables. The -tch is used when there is a short vowel before the /ch/ sound. Examples of these words include stitch, swatch, and watch.)
/E (Another /ch/ ending is represented by the -tch grapheme. This only comes at the ending of words or syllables. The -tch is used when there is a short vowel before the /ch/ sound. Examples of these words include stitch, swatch, and watch.)
/Pg 86 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
