4138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (* The suffix s can make three sounds: /s/, /z/, or /ez/. This depends on the phoneme that the base word of the suffix ends with. )
/E (* The suffix s can make three sounds: /s/, /z/, or /ez/. This depends on the phoneme that the base word of the suffix ends with. )
/Pg 97 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
4139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The -s makes the /s/ phoneme when there is a voiceless consonant that comes before the suffix. These letters are ones in which we do not feel a vibration in the throat when the sound is produced. These letters include p, t, c, k, q, f, h, s, and x. However, if a base word ends in s or x, the suffix will produces the /iz/ sound.)
/E (The -s makes the /s/ phoneme when there is a voiceless consonant that comes before the suffix. These letters are ones in which we do not feel a vibration in the throat when the sound is produced. These letters include p, t, c, k, q, f, h, s, and x. However, if a base word ends in s or x, the suffix will produces the /iz/ sound.)
/Pg 97 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
4140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The -s suffix makes the /z/ phoneme when there is a voiced consonant or a vowel at the end of the base word. The voiced consonants included b, d, g, j, l, m, n, ng, r, z, th \(voiced\), v, w, y, and z. These sounds can be felt on the throat when the sound is produced.)
/E (The -s suffix makes the /z/ phoneme when there is a voiced consonant or a vowel at the end of the base word. The voiced consonants included b, d, g, j, l, m, n, ng, r, z, th \(voiced\), v, w, y, and z. These sounds can be felt on the throat when the sound is produced.)
/Pg 97 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
4141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The -es suffix makes the /iz/ phoneme when the noun ends in the following consonants: -s, -x, -z, -sh, -ch. The suffix that will be used is -es with these words. This will produce the /iz/ sound. )
/E (The -es suffix makes the /iz/ phoneme when the noun ends in the following consonants: -s, -x, -z, -sh, -ch. The suffix that will be used is -es with these words. This will produce the /iz/ sound. )
/Pg 97 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
4142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Sometimes the addition of a suffix can add a singular sound, but sometimes it makes the word gain a syllable. Talk through these words as you begin to create using the suffix. )
/E (Sometimes the addition of a suffix can add a singular sound, but sometimes it makes the word gain a syllable. Talk through these words as you begin to create using the suffix. )
/Pg 97 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
